    {
      "title": "Scaling Assessment",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## How to Read This Dashboard\n\n**After 1-2 weeks of data collection**, use these panels to make scaling decisions:\n\n### Key Indicators\n| Metric | Green (Safe to Scale) | Yellow (Caution) | Red (Upgrade First) |\n|--------|----------------------|-------------------|---------------------|\n| CPU Headroom | >50% idle | 20-50% idle | <20% idle |\n| Memory Headroom | >30% available | 15-30% available | <15% available |\n| Swap Pressure | 0 ops/s | 1-50 ops/s | >50 ops/s |\n| OpenWebUI Memory | <70% of limit | 70-85% of limit | >85% of limit |\n| Request Queue Time | <1s P95 | 1-5s P95 | >5s P95 |\n| In-Flight Requests | <25 | 25-50 | >50 |\n\n### Scaling Projection\n1. **Observe** the daily request volume trend to estimate growth rate\n2. **Correlate** in-flight requests with CPU/memory to find the per-user resource cost\n3. **Check** the 30-day memory projections \u2014 if they hit the limit line, you need a bigger VM before scaling\n4. **Monitor** swap pressure \u2014 any sustained swapping means the VM is undersized for current load\n\n### Current VM: 6 cores / 16GB RAM\n- **1000 users**: Likely needs 32GB RAM (OpenWebUI memory is the bottleneck)\n- **5000 users**: Likely needs 64GB+ RAM and 12+ cores, or horizontal scaling"
      },
      "id": 12
    }
